.TH CHIMEDITOR 1 "November 2026" "ChimEditor 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chimeditor \- terminal-based non-linear video/audio editor and skip-cutter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chimeditor
[\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chimeditor
is a lightweight, terminal-based non-linear audio and video editor designed for
rapid review, trimming, and cutting of media files using intuitive keyboard controls.
.PP
ChimEditor provides real-time multi-speed playback (including reverse scrubbing),
dynamic playhead navigation, and instant skip-list creation. Skip sections are
automatically bypassed during playback and seeking. When exporting, ChimEditor
invokes FFmpeg with an optimized single-pass frame-selection filter graph to output
a synchronized file containing only the non-skipped media.
.PP
ChimEditor operates directly in the terminal using raw console mode with zero
external GUI dependencies.
.SH PROJECT FILES (.cme)
ChimEditor uses self-contained project archives with the
.B .cme
extension. A
.B .cme
file is a standard ZIP archive stored without re-compression (\fB-0\fR store mode)
that bundles:
.IP 1. 4
The original, unmodified source media file.
.IP 2. 4
A \fBskips.txt\fR metadata file recording all marked skip intervals.
.PP
.SS Creating a Project
When
.B chimeditor
is invoked with a media file (for example, \fImovie.mp4\fR or \fIclip.webm\fR):
.PP
.RS
.B chimeditor
\fImovie.mp4\fR
.RE
.PP
ChimEditor automatically packages the media file and an initial blank
\fBskips.txt\fR into \fImovie.cme\fR. The media opens immediately for editing.
All subsequent skip marks created during the session are written directly into
the \fImovie.cme\fR project file.
.PP
.SS Reopening an Existing Project
When
.B chimeditor
is invoked with a \fB.cme\fR project file:
.PP
.RS
.B chimeditor
\fImovie.cme\fR
.RE
.PP
ChimEditor opens the project archive, restores all previously saved skip ranges,
and extracts the packaged media to temporary storage for playback and export.
When ChimEditor exits, temporary extraction files are automatically deleted.
.SH KEYBOARD CONTROLS
ChimEditor is entirely keyboard-driven. Keybindings can be customized in
\fBconfig.yaml\fR.
.SS Playback and Speed Controls
.TP
.B Space
Toggle playback between play and pause.
.TP
.BR z ", " Z
Reset playback speed back to normal (1.0x).
.TP
.B Up Arrow
Increase playback speed by \fBspeed_step\fR (default: +0.5x).
.TP
.B Down Arrow
Decrease playback speed by \fBspeed_step\fR (default: -0.5x).
.TP
.BR f ", " F
Fast forward playback at \fBfast_forward_speed\fR (default: 2.0x).
.TP
.BR r ", " R
Reverse playback scrubbing at \fBreverse_speed\fR (default: -1.0x).
.SS Navigation and Playhead
.TP
.B Left Arrow
Seek backward by \fBseek_step_seconds\fR (default: 5.0 seconds).
Existing skip sections are bypassed seamlessly without consuming seek distance.
.TP
.B Right Arrow
Seek forward by \fBseek_step_seconds\fR (default: 5.0 seconds).
Existing skip sections are bypassed seamlessly.
.TP
.B Home
Jump immediately to the beginning of the file (00:00:00).
.TP
.B End
Jump immediately to the end of the file and pause playback.
.TP
.BR p ", " P
Display the current playhead timestamp and total duration in the top-left status
line in \fBHH:MM:SS / HH:MM:SS\fR format.
.TP
.BR w ", " W
Display the current playhead timestamp in words on the top-left status line (e.g.
\fB15 minutes 32 seconds\fR or \fB1 hour 15 minutes 32 seconds\fR). Hours are
omitted when the current timestamp is less than one hour.
.SS Skip Marking and Cutting
.TP
.B b
Mark the start of a skip interval at the current playhead position. The timestamp
is displayed at the top-left corner of the screen.
.TP
.B e
Mark the end of a skip interval at the current playhead position. Pairs with the
preceding \fBb\fR mark, automatically orders timestamps, merges any overlapping
or adjacent skip ranges, updates the real-time audio playback engine, and persists
the change to the \fB.cme\fR project file. The resulting interval
(\fBHH:MM:SS -> HH:MM:SS\fR) is displayed on the status line.
.TP
.B B \fR(Shift+B)\fP
Cut from beginning: immediately creates a skip interval from the start of the
file (\fB00:00:00\fR) to the current playhead position. Automatically merges with
existing skips, updates playback, and saves to the project file. Useful for trimming
intros or pre-roll banter with a single keystroke.
.TP
.B E \fR(Shift+E)\fP
Cut to end: immediately creates a skip interval from the current playhead position
to the end of the file (\fBduration\fR). Automatically merges with existing skips,
updates playback, and saves to the project file. Useful for trimming outros or
post-show commentary with a single keystroke.
.TP
.B A \fR(Shift+A)\fP
Toggle editing mode. When editing mode is active, ChimEditor does not jump over
or bypass skip intervals during playback. Instead, it plays through the entire
timeline continuously, sounding a synthesized ascending chime (400 Hz to 850 Hz)
at the beginning of each skip interval and a descending chime (850 Hz to 400 Hz)
at the end of each skip interval. This allows precise auditory verification of cut
points. Pressing \fBA\fR again disables editing mode and restores normal skipping.
.TP
.BR d ", " D
Delete skip under playhead. When editing mode is active and the playhead is inside a
skip interval, pressing \fBd\fR immediately removes that skip interval, updates the
playback engine, and persists the change to the \fB.cme\fR project file. If ChimEditor
is not in editing mode or the playhead is not within a skip, a status message is
displayed and no change is made.
.TP
.B n
Nudge beginning of current edit 0.25 seconds earlier (when in editing mode).
Moves the start boundary of the current skip interval 0.25 seconds earlier
and automatically seeks playback to 2 seconds before the new start boundary
(\fB00:00:00\fR if within 2 seconds of the beginning) so the editor can immediately
audition the revised cut point.
.TP
.B m
Nudge beginning of current edit 0.25 seconds later (when in editing mode).
Moves the start boundary of the current skip interval 0.25 seconds later
and automatically seeks playback to 2 seconds before the new start boundary.
.TP
.B N \fR(Shift+N)\fP
Nudge end of current edit 0.25 seconds earlier (when in editing mode).
Moves the end boundary of the current skip interval 0.25 seconds earlier
and automatically seeks playback to 2 seconds before the new end boundary
(\fB00:00:00\fR if within 2 seconds of the beginning) so the editor can immediately
audition the revised end cut point with the descending boundary chime.
.TP
.B M \fR(Shift+M)\fP
Nudge end of current edit 0.25 seconds later (when in editing mode).
Moves the end boundary of the current skip interval 0.25 seconds later
and automatically seeks playback to 2 seconds before the new end boundary.
.TP
.B C \fR(Shift+C)\fP
Cycle through skip sections: jumps the playhead to 2 seconds before the first skip section.
If the first skip starts at or within 2 seconds of the beginning of the file, jumps to the 0 play position (00:00:00).
Each subsequent press of \fBC\fR advances the playhead to 2 seconds before the next skip section.
If the current skip is the last one, pressing \fBC\fR cycles back to the first skip section.
.SS Export and Termination
.TP
.BR o ", " O
Export non-skipped media using FFmpeg. Pauses playback, silences the audio device,
and generates an edited media file in the project directory
(\fI<basename>-edited.<output_format>\fR for video outputs, or
\fI<basename>.<output_format>\fR without \fB-edited\fR for audio outputs). Displays
real-time export status on the screen and quits upon completion.
.TP
.BR q ", " Q ", " Esc
Save all skip ranges to the project file and quit ChimEditor.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Force quit the application.
.SH STATUS DISPLAY
ChimEditor reserves the top row (row 0, column 0) of the terminal screen for
live feedback:
.IP \(bu 2
Pressing \fBb\fR displays the marked start position (e.g. \fB00:01:15\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Pressing \fBe\fR, \fBB\fR, or \fBE\fR displays the created skip interval
(e.g. \fB00:01:15 -> 00:02:40\fR or \fB00:00:00 -> 00:00:45\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Pressing \fBA\fR displays \fBEditing mode: ON\fR or \fBEditing mode: OFF\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
Pressing \fBd\fR displays the deleted skip interval (e.g. \fBDeleted: 00:01:15 -> 00:02:40\fR),
\fBNot in edit mode\fR, or \fBNot inside a skip\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
Pressing \fBn\fR, \fBm\fR, \fBN\fR, or \fBM\fR displays the revised skip interval
(e.g. \fB00:01:14 -> 00:02:40\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Pressing \fBC\fR displays skip cycle status (e.g. \fBSkip 1/3: 00:00:08\fR) or \fBNo skips\fR if no skips are defined.
.IP \(bu 2
Pressing \fBp\fR displays current playhead progress
(e.g. \fB00:03:12 / 00:45:00\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Pressing \fBw\fR displays current playhead timestamp in words
(e.g. \fB15 minutes 32 seconds\fR or \fB1 hour 15 minutes 32 seconds\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Pressing \fBo\fR displays export status: \fBExporting <file>...\fR, followed by
\fBSaved <file>\fR upon success or \fBExport failed\fR if FFmpeg encounters an error.
.SH CONFIGURATION
ChimEditor loads configuration settings from \fB~/.config/shimeditor/config.yaml\fR
(or \fBconfig.yaml\fR in the current working directory if present).
If the configuration file does not exist, ChimEditor automatically creates
\fB~/.config/shimeditor/config.yaml\fR seeded with the complete default configuration.
.PP
.SS Structure of config.yaml
.nf
# Keybindings map action names to lists of key identifiers
keybindings:
  play_pause:              ["space"]
  normal_speed:            ["z", "Z"]
  speed_up:                ["up"]
  speed_down:              ["down"]
  fast_forward:            ["f", "F"]
  reverse:                 ["r", "R"]
  seek_backward:           ["left"]
  seek_forward:            ["right"]
  seek_beginning:          ["home"]
  seek_end:                ["end"]
  display_position:        ["p", "P"]
  display_timestamp_words: ["w", "W"]
  mark_skip_start:         ["b"]
  skip_from_beginning:     ["B"]
  mark_skip_end:           ["e"]
  skip_to_end:             ["E"]
  toggle_editing_mode:     ["A"]
  delete_skip:             ["d", "D"]
  cycle_skips:             ["C"]
  nudge_start_earlier:     ["n"]
  nudge_start_later:       ["m"]
  nudge_end_earlier:       ["N"]
  nudge_end_later:         ["M"]
  export:                  ["o", "O"]
  quit:                    ["q", "Q", "esc"]

# Operational settings
settings:
  # Container format for exported video/audio (default: "mp4")
  output_format: "mp4"

  # Speed step adjustment for Up/Down arrows
  speed_step: 0.5

  # Seek step in seconds for Left/Right arrows
  seek_step_seconds: 5.0

  # Fast forward multiplier
  fast_forward_speed: 2.0

  # Reverse playback multiplier
  reverse_speed: -1.0

  # Diagnostic log path
  log_file: "chimeditor.log"
.fi
.PP
.SS Supported Key Names
Single character keys (\fB"space"\fR, \fB"z"\fR, \fB"b"\fR, \fB"B"\fR, etc.) and
special named keys (\fB"left"\fR, \fB"right"\fR, \fB"up"\fR, \fB"down"\fR,
\fB"home"\fR, \fB"end"\fR, \fB"esc"\fR, \fB"enter"\fR, \fB"tab"\fR,
\fB"backspace"\fR, \fB"pageup"\fR, \fB"pagedown"\fR, and \fB"f1"\fR through \fB"f12"\fR).
.SH EXPORT MECHANISM
When the export command (\fBo\fR) is executed:
.IP 1. 4
Playback and audio output streams are paused to prevent ALSA/audio buffer underruns.
.IP 2. 4
Playable (non-skipped) time segments are calculated from the file duration and
merged skip list.
.IP 3. 4
If the media contains video, an optimized single-pass FFmpeg \fBselect\fR and
\fBaselect\fR filter graph is constructed:
.RS
.nf
-vf "select='between(t,s1,e1)+between(t,s2,e2)...',setpts=N/FRAME_RATE/TB"
-af "aselect='between(t,s1,e1)+between(t,s2,e2)...',asetpts=N/SR/TB"
.fi
.RE
This single-pass design avoids multi-branch buffering, keeping memory consumption
under 1 GB regardless of file length and avoiding out-of-memory errors on long 1080p/4K files.
.IP 4. 4
The resulting file is saved as \fI<basename>-edited.<output_format>\fR for video outputs (or \fI<basename>.<output_format>\fR without \fB-edited\fR for audio outputs) in the directory
containing the project archive.
.IP 5. 4
The full FFmpeg command, stream parameters, and encoding progress are logged to
\fBchimeditor.log\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/shimeditor/config.yaml
User application configuration file for keybindings and playback settings.
.TP
.B ~/.config/shimeditor/chimeditor.log
Diagnostic log recording FFprobe stream details, decoding metrics, FFmpeg export
commands, and operational events.
.TP
.B skips.txt
Plaintext skip list formatted as comma-separated timestamp pairs (packaged inside \fB.cme\fR):
.RS
.nf
# ChimEditor skip list
# Format: start_time,end_time

00:00:00,00:00:30
00:05:12,00:06:45
00:15:00,00:15:30
.fi
.RE
.TP
.I <name>.cme
ChimEditor project archive containing the source media and internal \fBskips.txt\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.B Example 1: Start a new project from an MP4 video
.RS
.B chimeditor video.mp4
.PP
Creates \fIvideo.cme\fR containing \fIvideo.mp4\fR and a blank skip list. Opens the
video for playback.
.RE
.PP
.B Example 2: Resume editing an existing project
.RS
.B chimeditor video.cme
.PP
Opens \fIvideo.cme\fR, restoring all previously defined skip intervals and loading
the packaged video stream.
.RE
.PP
.B Example 3: Quick intro and outro cut
.RS
1. Start playback and press \fBSpace\fR or \fBR\fR/\fBF\fR to locate the end of the intro.
.br
2. Press \fBB\fR to mark everything from the beginning to the current point as skipped.
.br
3. Scrub near the end of the video to locate where the outro begins.
.br
4. Press \fBE\fR to mark everything from the current point to the end as skipped.
.br
5. Press \fBo\fR to render the trimmed video to \fIvideo-edited.mp4\fR.
.RE
.PP
.B Example 4: Remove a segment in the middle
.RS
1. Position playhead where the unwanted section starts and press \fBb\fR.
.br
2. Position playhead where the unwanted section ends and press \fBe\fR.
.br
3. Playback immediately skips this range during playback and seeking.
.br
4. Press \fBq\fR to save the project and exit.
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATH
Must include standard command-line tools: \fBffmpeg\fR(1) and \fBffprobe\fR(1) for
media decoding/export, and \fBzip\fR(1) / \fBunzip\fR(1) (or \fBpython3\fR(1)) for
\fB.cme\fR archive management.
